            <ArticleTitle>Measuring asthma self-management knowledge in adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>530-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To present the development and psychometrics of a brief asthma self-management questionnaire for adults incorporating the five content areas considered essential for asthma self-management by the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DATA SOURCES" NlmCategory="METHODS">After development of the criterion-referenced questionnaire, determination of content validity, pilot testing, and revision, the questionnaire was administered to 305 adults with asthma.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">After exploratory principal component factor analysis, the final 24-item questionnaire had a reliability of .69, close to the preferred reliability of .70.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The questionnaire is recommended for assessing self-management knowledge in clinical settings and for evaluation of asthma education programs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
